<BaseLayout title="Tires and wheels">
  <h1>Tires and wheels</h1>
  <p>Wheel and tire fitment depends on the installed package and chassis. Use the tire-pressure and certification labels on the car as the authority for the wheels and tires actually fitted.</p>

  <figure class="diagram tpms-figure">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 240 160" role="img" aria-labelledby="tpms-title tpms-desc">
      <title id="tpms-title">Simplified tire-pressure warning symbol</title>
      <desc id="tpms-desc">A horseshoe-shaped tire cross-section with an exclamation mark, representing a low tire-pressure warning.</desc>
      <path d="M54 112 C55 65 74 28 120 28 C166 28 185 65 186 112" fill="none" stroke="#28536d" stroke-width="15" stroke-linecap="round" />
      <path d="M54 112 L54 126 M186 112 L186 126" fill="none" stroke="#28536d" stroke-width="15" stroke-linecap="round" />
      <path d="M120 57 V91" stroke="#b18a43" stroke-width="11" stroke-linecap="round" />
      <circle cx="120" cy="112" r="6" fill="#b18a43" />
    </svg>
    <figcaption>Schematic representation of the low tire-pressure warning symbol. It is not an exact instrument-cluster reproduction; read the driver-display message and consult Volvo's <a href="https://www.volvocars.com/en-sa/support/car/s60/20w17/article/73e14f8cc7f8d151c0a81f6f7932e5d8/c16e2a6e902332cac0a8cc8a37f81057/22daa2aac8ee9cb4c0a8cc8e62e73faf/1eab27e792f46d8ec0a8015149fd35c7/">2021 S60 tire-pressure guidance</a>.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h2>Record the installed setup</h2>
  <table>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th>Tire brand and model</th><td>Record from sidewall</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Front tire size</th><td>Record from sidewall</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Rear tire size</th><td>Record from sidewall; confirm whether staggered</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Load index and speed rating</th><td>Record from sidewall</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Wheel diameter and width</th><td>Record from wheel marking or parts documentation</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Cold inflation pressure</th><td>Use the driver's-door/B-pillar tire placard for the installed tire and load condition</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Pressure checks</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Check pressure when tires are cold, ideally before driving.</li>
    <li>Use a reliable pressure gauge; do not bleed air from a warm tire to reach the cold specification.</li>
    <li>Check all four tires at least monthly and before long trips.</li>
    <li>Inspect tread and sidewalls for uneven wear, cuts, bulges, cracking, or embedded objects.</li>
    <li>After adjusting pressure, follow the vehicle's instructions for storing/resetting the tire-pressure monitoring reference value. On the 2021 S60, Volvo's owner information describes storing a new reference value through the center display; the vehicle may need to be driven above 35 km/h (22 mph) for several minutes before the value is saved.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Rotation and replacement</h2>
  <p>Follow the tire manufacturer's rotation guidance and Volvo's restrictions for the specific wheel/tire combination. Directional tires, staggered fitments, and different front/rear sizes limit rotation options. Match replacement tires for size, load index, speed rating, construction, and suitability for the drivetrain.</p>

  <h2>Jack and wheel work</h2>
  <p>Use only the designated lifting points and a stable, level surface. Chock the wheels that remain on the ground. Never work under a vehicle supported only by a jack. Confirm wheel-fastener torque from the correct Volvo service information for the installed wheel and fastener.</p>

